## The 5 ledgers you need (one-time setup — already done for you)

| Ledger | Category (Group) | What it represents |
|---|---|---|
| **Kanpur Bahraich Forwarding** | Transporters (a folder I made under "Sundry Debtors") | The transporter who owes you money |
| **Kanpur Branch Cash (Galla)** | Cash-in-Hand | Physical cash in your branch's cash box |
| **Kanpur Branch Bank Account** | Bank Accounts | Your branch's bank account |
| **PF Income** | Direct Incomes | **Income that comes FROM transporters** (their PF/freight settlement — the crossing-bill kind of income) |
| **Delivery Income** | Direct Incomes | A *separate* ledger for income that does NOT come from transporters (e.g. door-delivery charges collected directly from a consignee) — kept, but unused in this example |

**Important correction:** income received from a transporter goes to **PF
Income**, not Delivery Income — those are two different revenue streams
for you, and mixing them would make both numbers wrong. I originally
credited Delivery Income by mistake in the first draft of this example;
it's now fixed (see the correction note below).

You make these **once per transporter / once per branch**, not once per
bill or once per payment. From now on, every August bill, every payment,
every future transporter — you just create more bills and vouchers
against these same ledgers. You will NOT be creating a new ledger for
every transaction — only for every new person/account.

